# Multi-Tenancy & Routing Architecture (CRITICAL)

The `store-front` application is a multi-tenant platform where each merchant storefront is resolved dynamically via subdomain.

## 1. Subdomain Resolution & Multi-Tenancy Flow

```
HTTP Request (Host: storeA.cash-vio.com)
  │
  ├── 1. middleware.ts: Parses subdomain with getStoreSubdomain(hostname)
  │      - Validates against RESERVED_SUBDOMAINS ('www', 'api', 'admin', etc.)
  │      - Enforces root-only access on main/apex domain
  │      - Attaches locale and visitor cookies
  │      - Forwards ?lang= and theme preview headers
  │
  ├── 2. resolveRequestStore() (React.cache per-request deduplication):
  │      - Reads Host header
  │      - Calls getStoreBySubdomain(subdomain) (cached 60s with unstable_cache)
  │      - Invokes setApiStoreId(store.id) & setApiLocale(locale)
  │
  └── 3. API Requests via apiClient:
         - Automatically attach header: X-Store-Id: <store-id>
         - Automatically attach header: Accept-Language: <en|ar>
```

## 2. Invariant Store Context Rules

- **Never bypass `resolveRequestStore()`**: Server components, layouts, and `generateMetadata` must always resolve store context via `resolveRequestStore()` in `src/lib/api/resolve-request-store.ts`.
- **Never query without `X-Store-Id`**: All public backend queries (`/public/products`, `/public/categories`, `/public/orders`, etc.) require `X-Store-Id`. In client components, `StoreProvider` and the layout inline script ensure `window.__STORE_ID__` and cookie `sf_store_id` are populated.
- **Inactive Storefront Gate**: When `store.storeFront.status !== StoreFrontStatus.ACTIVE`, `src/app/layout.tsx` must immediately render `StoreErrorComponent` (type `INACTIVE`) and prevent browsing or purchasing.

```typescript
// ❌ FORBIDDEN — Calling API directly without resolving store context
export default async function ProductPage({ params }: { params: { id: string } }) {
  const product = await apiClient.get(`/public/products/${params.id}`); // Missing X-Store-Id!
  return <div>{product.name}</div>;
}

// ✅ REQUIRED — Resolving store context and handling notFound
export default async function ProductPage({ params }: ProductPageProps) {
  const { store, subdomain } = await resolveRequestStore();
  if (!subdomain || !store) {
    throw new Error("Invalid store subdomain");
  }

  const { id } = await params;
  const { product, error } = await getProductByIdWithErrorHandling(id);
  if (error || !product) {
    notFound();
  }

  return <ProductDetails product={product} storeId={store.id} ... />;
}
```

## 3. App Router Structure & Rendering Invariants

- **Single Root Layout**: `src/app/layout.tsx` is the sole application shell. There are no nested segment layouts or `template.tsx` files.
- **Dynamic Rendering**: `src/app/layout.tsx` explicitly declares:
  ```typescript
  export const dynamic = "force-dynamic";
  export const revalidate = 0;
  ```
- **Loading Skeletons (`loading.tsx`)**: Every major route segment MUST provide a dedicated `loading.tsx` skeleton mirroring the exact geometry of the rendered page (`/`, `/products`, `/products/[id]`, `/categories`, `/categories/[id]`, `/cart`, `/checkout`, `/pages/[slug]`).
- **Error Boundaries**:
  - `src/app/error.tsx`: Root client error boundary with retry capability.
  - `src/app/not-found.tsx`: Global 404 handler invoked via Next.js `notFound()`.
- **Parallel Data Fetching**: Independent server-side fetches must NEVER be awaited in series. Always execute them in parallel using `Promise.all` or `Promise.allSettled`.

```typescript
// ❌ FORBIDDEN — Sequential awaiting in Server Component
const categories = await getCategories();
const products = await getProducts();
const specialProducts = await getSpecialProducts();

// ✅ REQUIRED — Parallel execution
const [categoriesData, productsData, specialData] = await Promise.all([
  getCategoriesWithErrorHandling({ page: 1, limit: 12 }),
  getProductsWithErrorHandling({ page: 1, limit: 12 }),
  getSpecialProductsWithErrorHandling(),
]);
```
